{"ts": "2026-10-27T13:59:52.878888Z", "run_id": "r-20261027T1359Z-b357", "unit": "openspec:add-audit-chain", "seq": 8, "type": "task.started", "task": "1.1", "title": "1.1 Write `src/audit/canonical.test.ts` first (scenarios \"RFC 8785 vectors\" and \"Refused values\"; the refused inputs as a table of `[value, reason]` pairs, each checked with `assert.throws(fn, { code: \"AUDIT_CANONICAL_INVALID\" })` and `error.details.reason`), then implement `AuditError` and `AuditErrorCode` and the module-internal `wrapStoreError` in `src/audit/errors.ts`, and `canonicalize` in `src/audit/canonical.ts`, both exported through `src/audit/index.ts` (`wrapStoreError` not). `wrapStoreError(err)` returns `new AuditError(\"AUDIT_STORE_FAILED\", \"audit store failed\", { sqlstate })` when `err` is an object whose `code` is a string of exactly five characters from `0-9A-Z`, else `err` itself. `canonicalize` walks recursively with `depth` = the number of enclosing containers: an array or object entered at `depth >= 64` is `too_deep`; `null`, booleans and finite numbers (`Object.is(v, -0) ? \"0\" : JSON.stringify(v)`); a string needs `isWellFormed()` (`ill_formed_string`) and no U+0000 (`nul`) and is written with `JSON.stringify`; a bigint within `Number.MIN_SAFE_INTEGER` to `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER` is `v.toString()`, else `bigint_range`; `undefined`, functions and symbols are refused with their reason, `NaN` is `nan`, `±Infinity` `infinity`; arrays are read by index (a hole reads as `undefined`); objects must have prototype `Object.prototype` or `null` (`not_plain_object`), keys from `Object.keys` sorted with the default `sort()` (UTF-16 order) and each key checked like a string. Every error is `AuditError(\"AUDIT_CANONICAL_INVALID\", \"value cannot be canonicalized\", { reason })`, implementing requirement \"One canonicalization function\""}
